ng for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply\n\n⚠️ [... middle content omitted — showing head and tail ...]\n\n reportedly the preferred cryptocurrency.\\n\\nCryptoTimes says Iran has launched a state-backed digital insurance platform that turns one of the world's most strategically important shipping lanes into a cryptocurrency-settled business. The platform, called Hormuz Safe, issues digital maritime insurance policies for commercial vessels transiting the Persian Gulf, the Strait of Hormuz, and surrounding waterways, with premiums paid and settled in Bitcoin. The initiative was first reported on May 16, 2026, by Fars News Agency, an outlet affiliated with Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, citing a document obtained from Iran's Ministry of Economic Affairs and Finance.\\n\\nThe CryptoTimes article emphasizes that the Strait of Hormuz is the single most important chokepoint in the global energy trade. Roughly 20% of the world's daily oil supply passes through the narrow channel between Iran and Oman. Every tanker and cargo vessel navigating that corridor requires marine insurance, and those policies have traditionally been underwritten and settled through Western financial institutions that Iran, under years of sanctions, is largely cut off from. Hormuz Safe is designed to route around exactly that problem.\\n\\nAccording to the Ministry's framework, the platform offers shipping companies and independent cargo owners fast-track, cryptographically verifiable insurance policies. The operational protocol functions through a streamlined on-chain sequence: premium settlement, where a vessel operator selects a custom risk tier and transmits the designated premium in Bitcoin to a state-controlled wallet ecosystem; instant coverage, where the moment the transaction receives immutable validation on the blockchain network, the maritime cargo is considered active and insured; and cryptographic proof, where the vessel owner is immediately issued a digitally signed receipt to serve as proof of coverage for foreign port authorities.\\n\\nCryptoTimes says the policy framework primarily covers the inspection, detention, and physical confiscation of vessels by regional actors. Direct damage from military or kinetic attacks is explicitly carved out of standard coverage terms. The Ministry also reportedly noted that the verification system is engineered to grant Tehran informational dominance over the corridor, allowing the state to identify and audit data from different transiting nations.\\n\\nThe article says Iranian officials estimate the platform could generate more than $10 billion in revenue, though that figure should be treated cautiously because the technical and legal specifications have not been fully disclosed. It also says the deployment of Bitcoin is a calculated geopolitical move: cut off from dollar-denominated clearing houses and the SWIFT messaging network, traditional premium routing would likely be flagged and blocked by Western compliance systems. Hormuz Safe, the piece argues, marks a shift from passive crypto holdings to active operational financial infrastructure.\\n\\nCryptoTimes also notes that the platform launches in an environment where insuring a Hormuz transit has become economically unviable for many operators. Since the outbreak of regional hostilities, war-risk insurance premiums have risen from standard pre-conflict baselines of 0.25% to as high as 5% to 10% of a vessel's total hull value per voyage. Under those conditions, a $100 million oil tanker could face a $10 million insurance charge just to cross the channel, creating an opening for Iran's crypto alternative. The article warns that sanctions exposure, lack of Western recognition, and scam risks remain major obstacles to the platform's practical adoption.\\n\\nTogether, the articles frame Hormuz Safe as a geopolitically charged experiment in using Bitcoin for state-level insurance settlement, maritime control, and sanctions-resistant financial infrastructure in one of the world's most important shipping corridors.\"\r\n}\r\nCHART_COIN: bitcoin\n\nProcess exited with code 0.[... 14064 more characters truncated]"}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"neat-shoal","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"\r\n[1m[38;5;209m🦞 OpenClaw[39m[22m [38;5;216m2026.4.23[39m [38;5;138m(a979721)[39m [38;5;138m—[39m [38;5;167mYour task has been queued; your dignity has been deprecated.[39m\r\n\r\n[?25l[90m│[39m\r\n[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m..[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m...[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m...[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaitin